LOCUS       fwd_two_exon             500 bp    DNA     circular SYN 28-APR-2026
DEFINITION  Synthetic plasmid for the strand-guard regression in
            applyComplementOriginWrap. NOT a real construct.
ACCESSION   fwd_two_exon_synth
VERSION     fwd_two_exon_synth
COMMENT     regression fixture for the forward-strand strand-guard.
            A two-exon forward-strand gene whose first exon happens to start
            at base 1 and whose last exon happens to end at the sequence
            length. Without the strand guard in applyComplementOriginWrap
            (and the matching guard in plasmid-viewer's parseGenBank
            post-pass), this CDS would be misclassified as a complement-
            strand origin-wrap and silently rewritten to start>end shape.
            Forward-strand origin-wraps are serialized in physical order
            (`join(451..500,1..50)`) and are caught by the per-location
            heuristic, not the post-pass.
FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     CDS             join(1..50,451..500)
                     /label="fwd_two_exon"
                     /note="forward-strand two-exon gene with boundary-
                     touching parts; must NOT be rewritten as a wrap"
